From fddc6d48ad702096d4cee76c72904202802ac5a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:32:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] ARM64: Make msvc_build/aarch64 build with current
 Visual Studio

Drop the x86/x64 solution platforms, use the installed toolset and
Windows SDK, build as a static library (FFI_STATIC_BUILD), add the
missing raw_api.c, java_raw_api.c and tramp.c sources, stop compiling
dlmalloc.c separately (closures.c includes it), and archive the
armasm64 object into the library.  Regenerate aarch64_include/ffi.h and
fficonfig.h from an ARM64 msvcc.sh configure of libffi 3.8.0, replacing
the stale 3.3-rc0 copies.
---
 msvc_build/aarch64/Ffi_staticLib.sln          |   8 -
 msvc_build/aarch64/Ffi_staticLib.vcxproj      |  33 ++--
 msvc_build/aarch64/aarch64_include/ffi.h      | 185 ++++++++++++------
 .../aarch64/aarch64_include/fficonfig.h       | 103 ++++------
 4 files changed, 188 insertions(+), 141 deletions(-)

